# Client routes — SCOPED, deliberately. No wildcard `/* /index.html
# 200`: a wildcard makes Cloudflare Pages answer every missing hashed
# asset with index.html as 200 text/html, which strict-MIME refuses and
# the immutable cache header then pins for a year. Adding a route in
# src/Route.elm means adding a line here by name, and that friction is
# the point. CI fails the build if a wildcard appears.

/about /index.html 200
/design-standard /index.html 200
